Falsifies `usb::verification::two_reports_produce_a_bounded_number_of_events`.

The defect: `changes` reports every modifier transition twice, once before the keys and once again
after the presses, as a debounce. The bound of twenty is the exact maximum (8 modifiers, 6 releases,
6 presses), so only a doubling bug can exceed it, and a flip of every modifier bit now costs sixteen
events.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(n <= 20)`.

